Zand move everything to its proper location.  The daemon must have
Zread and write access to the score files.
Z
Z
ZHow Search Works.
Z
ZThe entire i/o of the game is transmitted over messages.
ZThe screen output comes from the daemon, through the messages
Zto the player, and then to the screen.  The commands come from the
Zplayer to the daemon via that same message.
Z
ZScore is kept by the daemon, and the score file is updated by it
Zalso.  This results in a slight delay when a player exits the
Zgame.
Z
ZShould the daemon terminate for any reason, it is possible to look
Zin a file of errors that the daemon keeps.  While many of the entries
Zin this file will not be errors, it should give some sort of reason
Zwhy it died.  This file is (on our system) "/usr/games/lib/search/errlog".
Z
ZIf it at any time becomes necessary to kill the daemon, please do
Zso with "kill -INT pid" (not verifyed), as this will let the daemon "clean up"
Zafter itself.
